              "situation": "when_comparing",
              "verbatim": "couldn't stand how slow notion is",
              "cites": ["src:3"]
            }
          ],
          "costs_them": "Seconds on every open that add up to notes they never take.",
          "fears": "No source states a fear; the quotes stop at the annoyance and the switch.",
          "dream_outcome": "A notes tool that opens as fast as Google Docs."
        },
        "economic_buyer": {
          "says": [
            {
              "situation": "when_it_bites",
              "verbatim": "Knowing it would feel tedious to open Notion made me reconsider if the idea was worth writing down at all.",
              "cites": ["src:1"]
            }
          ],
          "costs_them": "Ideas the team never wrote down, and the cost of moving the wiki back to Google Workspace.",
          "fears": "That the wiki stays empty because nobody wants to open it.",
          "dream_outcome": "A wiki fast enough that writing a thing down costs nothing."
        }
      },
      "relief": {
        "line": "It's just there. The page is open before the thought is gone.",
        "says": [],
        "gap": "Searched HN comments only; no buyer described the after-state of a faster Notion, and review sites were blocked."
      },
      "euphoria": {
        "line": "Nothing gets lost. The team writes everything down because it costs nothing to.",
        "says": [],
        "gap": "No source; the euphoria search was not run past HN, which carried complaints only."
      },
